# US.ptiles Schema v7

Multi-layer timeline spatial data format. Extends v6's single-layer building format
to seven independent layers: buildings, roads, places, admin, water, rail, parks.

## Key Changes from v6

- Magic: `PTILEST\x00` (T = timeline, was F = footprints in v6)
- Version: 7
- Multi-layer: each layer has its own spatial index and data blocks
- New layer-specific record formats for non-building features
- Layer directory maps layer types to their index/block regions

## Compression

Same techniques as v6:
- Zstd dictionary compression (level 22): Shared dictionary across all layers
- Delta coordinate encoding: Zigzag + varint for vertex deltas
- Delta OSM ID encoding: Sequential IDs within H3 cells
- H3 spatial clustering: Features grouped by geographic cell
- Indexed type codes: Common types as 1-byte indices

## File Structure

```
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| Header (256 bytes)                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| Zstd Dictionary (variable, typically 512 KB)                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| Layer Directory (variable)                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| Spatial Index: Buildings                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| Data Blocks: Buildings                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| Spatial Index: Roads                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| Data Blocks: Roads                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
| ... (one index + blocks per layer)                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Header (256 bytes)

| Offset | Size | Type   | Field            | Description                    |
|--------|------|--------|------------------|--------------------------------|
| 0      | 8    | bytes  | magic            | `PTILEST\x00` (T = timeline)   |
| 8      | 1    | uint8  | version          | 7                              |
| 9      | 1    | uint8  | layer_count      | Number of layers present       |
| 10     | 6    | -      | reserved         | Padding                        |
| 16     | 4    | float  | min_lat          | Bounding box south             |
| 20     | 4    | float  | min_lon          | Bounding box west              |
| 24     | 4    | float  | max_lat          | Bounding box north             |
| 28     | 4    | float  | max_lon          | Bounding box east              |
| 32     | 8    | uint64 | total_poi_count  | Total features across layers   |
| 40     | 8    | uint64 | dict_offset      | Byte offset to dictionary      |
| 48     | 4    | uint32 | dict_length      | Dictionary size in bytes       |
| 52     | 8    | uint64 | layer_dir_offset | Byte offset to layer directory |
| 60     | 4    | uint32 | layer_dir_length | Layer directory size in bytes  |
| 64     | 192  | -      | reserved         | Future use (zeroed)            |

Byte order: Little-endian throughout.

## Layer Directory

| Offset | Size   | Type   | Field        | Description                 |
|--------|--------|--------|--------------|-----------------------------|
| 0      | 1      | uint8  | layer_count  | Number of layers            |
| 1      | 3      | -      | reserved     | Padding                     |
| 4+     | varies | -      | entries[]    | One entry per layer         |

Each entry:
| Offset | Size   | Type        | Field         | Description                  |
|--------|--------|-------------|---------------|------------------------------|
| 0      | 1      | uint8       | layer_type    | Layer enum (see below)       |
| 1      | 1      | uint8       | name_len      | Length of layer name         |
| 2      | varies | UTF-8       | name          | Layer name string            |
| -      | 8      | uint64      | index_offset  | Byte offset to spatial index |
| -      | 4      | uint32      | index_length  | Index size in bytes          |
| -      | 8      | uint64      | blocks_offset | Byte offset to first block   |
| -      | 8      | uint64      | poi_count     | Features in this layer       |

## Layer Types

| Index | Layer     | Geometry    | Description              |
|-------|-----------|-------------|--------------------------|
| 0     | buildings | Polygon     | Building footprints      |
| 1     | roads     | LineString  | Road centerlines         |
| 2     | places    | Point       | Cities, towns, villages  |
| 3     | admin     | Polygon     | Administrative boundaries |
| 4     | water     | Polygon     | Lakes, rivers, reservoirs|
| 5     | rail      | LineString  | Railway tracks           |
| 6     | parks     | Polygon     | Parks, gardens, reserves |
| 7-255 | reserved  | -           | Future use               |

## Spatial Index

Same format as v6 but per-layer. H3 resolution 7 cells sorted by H3 cell ID.

| Field        | Size | Type   | Description                    |
|--------------|------|--------|--------------------------------|
| entry_count  | 4    | uint32 | Number of index entries        |
| For each:    |      |        |                                |
| h3_cell      | 8    | uint64 | H3 index as integer            |
| block_offset | 6    | bytes  | Absolute byte offset to block  |
| block_length | 3    | bytes  | Compressed block size          |
| poi_count    | 2    | uint16 | Features in this cell          |

Entry size: 19 bytes (8 + 6 + 3 + 2).

## Layer Record Formats

### Buildings (layer 0)

Same binary format as v6. Polygons with building type, name, and optional metadata.

| Field       | Encoding          | Description                        |
|-------------|-------------------|------------------------------------|
| osm_id      | varint (delta)    | Delta from previous OSM ID         |
| vertex_count| uint8             | Polygon vertex count (max 255)     |
| first_lon   | int32             | First longitude in microdegrees    |
| first_lat   | int32             | First latitude in microdegrees     |
| deltas      | varint zigzag x2  | Vertex deltas (lon, lat per pair)  |
| flags       | uint8             | Bit flags for optional fields      |
| btype_idx   | uint8             | Building type index (0-19, 255)    |
| [btype_str] | uint8 + UTF-8     | Custom type if btype_idx == 255    |
| [name]      | uint16 + UTF-8    | Flag 0x01                          |
| [category]  | uint8 + UTF-8     | Flag 0x02                          |
| [name_src]  | uint8 + UTF-8     | Flag 0x04                          |
| [poi_osm_id]| uint64            | Flag 0x08                          |
| [height]    | uint8             | Flag 0x10 (0.5m steps)             |

### Roads (layer 1)

LineString geometry with highway classification.

| Field       | Encoding          | Description                        |
|-------------|-------------------|------------------------------------|
| osm_id      | varint (delta)    | Delta from previous OSM ID         |
| vertex_count| uint8             | Line vertices (max 255)            |
| first_lon   | int32             | First longitude in microdegrees    |
| first_lat   | int32             | First latitude in microdegrees     |
| deltas      | varint zigzag x2  | Vertex deltas                      |
| flags       | uint8             | Optional fields                    |
| rtype_idx   | uint8             | Road type index (0-23, 255)        |
| [rtype_str] | uint8 + UTF-8     | Custom type if rtype_idx == 255    |
| [name]      | uint16 + UTF-8    | Flag 0x01                          |
| [maxspeed]  | uint8             | Flag 0x02 (mph)                    |
| [layer_z]   | int8              | Flag 0x04 (bridge/tunnel level)    |

Road type index: motorway=0, trunk=1, primary=2, secondary=3, tertiary=4,
unclassified=5, residential=6, motorway_link=7, trunk_link=8, primary_link=9,
secondary_link=10, tertiary_link=11, living_street=12, service=13, pedestrian=14,
track=15, bus_guideway=16, escape=17, raceway=18, road=19, footway=20,
bridleway=21, steps=22, path=23.

### Places (layer 2)

Point geometry for populated places.

| Field       | Encoding          | Description                        |
|-------------|-------------------|------------------------------------|
| osm_id      | varint (delta)    | Delta from previous OSM ID         |
| lon         | int32             | Longitude in microdegrees          |
| lat         | int32             | Latitude in microdegrees           |
| flags       | uint8             | Optional fields                    |
| ptype_idx   | uint8             | Place type index (0-13, 255)       |
| [ptype_str] | uint8 + UTF-8     | Custom type if ptype_idx == 255    |
| name        | uint16 + UTF-8    | Always present                     |
| [population]| varint            | Flag 0x01                          |

Place type index: city=0, town=1, village=2, hamlet=3, suburb=4, quarter=5,
neighbourhood=6, isolated_dwelling=7, farm=8, county=9, state=10, country=11,
continent=12, locality=13.

### Admin (layer 3)

Polygon geometry for administrative boundaries.

| Field       | Encoding          | Description                        |
|-------------|-------------------|------------------------------------|
| osm_id      | varint (delta)    | Delta from previous OSM ID         |
| admin_level | uint8             | OSM admin_level (2-10)             |
| vertex_count| uint8             | Polygon vertices                   |
| first_lon   | int32             | First longitude in microdegrees    |
| first_lat   | int32             | First latitude in microdegrees     |
| deltas      | varint zigzag x2  | Vertex deltas                      |
| flags       | uint8             | Optional fields                    |
| name        | uint16 + UTF-8    | Always present                     |
| [iso_code]  | uint8 + UTF-8     | Flag 0x01                          |

### Water (layer 4)

Polygon geometry for water bodies.

| Field       | Encoding          | Description                        |
|-------------|-------------------|------------------------------------|
| osm_id      | varint (delta)    | Delta from previous OSM ID         |
| vertex_count| uint8             | Polygon vertices                   |
| first_lon   | int32             | First longitude in microdegrees    |
| first_lat   | int32             | First latitude in microdegrees     |
| deltas      | varint zigzag x2  | Vertex deltas                      |
| flags       | uint8             | Optional fields                    |
| wtype_idx   | uint8             | Water type index (0-11, 255)       |
| [wtype_str] | uint8 + UTF-8     | Custom type if wtype_idx == 255    |
| [name]      | uint16 + UTF-8    | Flag 0x01                          |

Water type index: lake=0, reservoir=1, river=2, stream=3, canal=4, pond=5,
basin=6, lagoon=7, oxbow=8, riverbank=9, wetland=10, bay=11.

### Rail (layer 5)

LineString geometry for railway tracks.

| Field       | Encoding          | Description                        |
|-------------|-------------------|------------------------------------|
| osm_id      | varint (delta)    | Delta from previous OSM ID         |
| vertex_count| uint8             | Line vertices                      |
| first_lon   | int32             | First longitude in microdegrees    |
| first_lat   | int32             | First latitude in microdegrees     |
| deltas      | varint zigzag x2  | Vertex deltas                      |
| flags       | uint8             | Optional fields                    |
| rtype_idx   | uint8             | Rail type index (0-10, 255)        |
| [rtype_str] | uint8 + UTF-8     | Custom type if rtype_idx == 255    |
| [name]      | uint16 + UTF-8    | Flag 0x01                          |

Rail type index: rail=0, light_rail=1, subway=2, tram=3, monorail=4,
narrow_gauge=5, funicular=6, disused=7, abandoned=8, preserved=9, miniature=10.

### Parks (layer 6)

Polygon geometry for parks, gardens, and natural areas.

| Field       | Encoding          | Description                        |
|-------------|-------------------|------------------------------------|
| osm_id      | varint (delta)    | Delta from previous OSM ID         |
| vertex_count| uint8             | Polygon vertices                   |
| first_lon   | int32             | First longitude in microdegrees    |
| first_lat   | int32             | First latitude in microdegrees     |
| deltas      | varint zigzag x2  | Vertex deltas                      |
| flags       | uint8             | Optional fields                    |
| ptype_idx   | uint8             | Park type index (0-13, 255)        |
| [ptype_str] | uint8 + UTF-8     | Custom type if ptype_idx == 255    |
| [name]      | uint16 + UTF-8    | Flag 0x01                          |

Park type index: park=0, garden=1, nature_reserve=2, national_park=3,
recreation_ground=4, playground=5, pitch=6, sports_centre=7, cemetery=8,
common=9, forest=10, grass=11, meadow=12, wood=13.

## Shared Binary Encoding

### Varint

Protobuf-style unsigned varint: 7 bits per byte, MSB indicates continuation.

### Zigzag

Maps signed integers to unsigned for efficient varint encoding:
  zigzag(n) = (n << 1) ^ (n >> 63)

### Delta coordinates

Each subsequent vertex encoded as:
  delta_lon = zigzag(current_lon - previous_lon)
  delta_lat = zigzag(current_lat - previous_lat)

## Data Block Format

Each block is zstd compressed (level 22) with shared dictionary.

Decompressed format:
```
+-----------------------------+
| record_length (4 bytes)     |
| record_data (variable)      |
+-----------------------------+
| record_length (4 bytes)     |
| record_data (variable)      |
+-----------------------------+
| ...                         |
+-----------------------------+
```

Records within a block are sorted by OSM ID for delta encoding efficiency.

## Version History

| Version | Changes                                                    |
|---------|------------------------------------------------------------|
| **7**   | **Multi-layer: 7 layer types with per-layer indexes**      |
| 6       | Buildings only: delta OSM IDs + zigzag varint coords       |
| 5       | Buildings only: varint coords, full OSM IDs                |
| 4       | Buildings only: binary footprints, fixed-size coords       |
| 3       | Buildings only: JSON minimal format (gzip)                 |

## Reference Implementation

| Language | File    | Notes                     |
|----------|---------|---------------------------|
| Rust     | ptiles-v7/ | Reader library (this crate) |

## Dependencies

- Rust 2021 edition
- `byteorder` (little-endian binary I/O)
- `zstd` (zstd decompression with dictionary)
- `integer-encoding` (varint utilities)
- `h3o` (H3 spatial indexing bindings)
